  "facts": [
    "Gladesville Bridge, opened 2 October 1964, was the longest single‑span concrete arch in the world at 277 metres, a record that still stands today.",
    "The bridge’s design, championed by Guy Maunsell, Anthony Gee, and famed precast pioneer Eugène Freyssinet, stretched to 305 metres and was built by Reed & Mallik with Stuart Brothers.",
    "Construction employed a novel inflatable‑gasket technique, where hollow precast blocks were lifted, gaskets inflated to lift the arch, then filled with concrete to lock the shape."
  ],
